mdr: command-line client for the Modrinth API
Agents: run "mdr schema" for a machine-readable command list.

Usage:
  mdr <command> [flags]

Commands:
  search       Search projects
  project      Read, create and edit projects (mods, modpacks, ...)
  version      Read, download, upload and edit versions
  file         Look up versions by file hash (local mod files)
  user         Read users
  team         Read teams
  tag          Read tags (categories, loaders, game versions, licenses)
  stats        Show site-wide counts of projects, versions, files, authors
  auth         Manage the saved API token
  config       Read and change settings in config.json
  api          Call any API endpoint and print the response
  completion   Print a shell completion script
  schema       Describe commands as JSON (for agents and scripts)

Global flags:
  -o, --output <auto|json|ndjson|table>   output format; auto: table on a terminal, json otherwise;
                                          do not parse table (default auto)
      --fields <a,b.c>                    select output fields (comma-separated paths, or all)
      --full                              output all fields (same as --fields all)
      --staging                           use the staging API (staging-api.modrinth.com)
      --dry-run                           print the request that would be sent instead of sending it
  -y, --yes                               skip the confirmation of destructive commands
      --timeout <seconds>                 per-request timeout in seconds, 1-3600 (default 30)
      --max-wait <seconds>                max seconds to wait on rate limits in total, 0-3600
                                          (default 60)
      --no-retry                          disable automatic retries
  -v, --verbose                           log requests to stderr
  -vv                                     log requests and headers to stderr
  -q, --quiet                             suppress notes on stderr (errors are still printed)
      --no-color                          disable colors (also NO_COLOR)
  -h, --help                              show help
      --version                           print the mdr version

Run "mdr <command> --help" for details.
